    <title>Policy Sheet</title>

    <p>
      This is the syllabus for <term>Fundamentals of Data Science Methods (CMSE 381)</term> for [Fall] 2026.
      It is a [4] credit course.
      <!-- use a description list (dl) for short items -->
      <dl>
        <li>
          <title>Instructor</title>

          <p>
            Prof. Firas Khasawneh, Ph.D. (Dr. K), EB 2503, <url href="mailto:khasawn3@msu.edu">khasawn3@msu.edu</url>.
          </p>
        </li>            
          
        <li>
          <title>Instructor</title>

          <p>
            Liangzhang Bao, Ph.D., EB 2507L, <url href="mailto:baolianz@msu.edu">baolianz@msu.edu</url>.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <title>Office hours</title>

          <p>
            TBD
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <title>Class meets</title>

          <p>
            Section 001 (Dr. K): MWF 3:30-4:40 PM at Olds Hall 109
          </p>
          <p>
            Section 002 (Dr. Bao): MWF 12:30-1:40 PM at Holden Hall C135
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <title>Course Description</title>

          <p>
            CMSE 381 is an introduction course to statistical and machine learning. It covers the fundamentals of data science methods, including unsupervised learning and supervised learning, feature extraction, dimension reduction, clustering, regression and classification.
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <title>Prerequisite</title>

          <p>
            (STT 180 and MTH 314 and CMSE 201 and STT 380)
          </p>
          <p>
             or (STT 180 and MTH 314 and CMSE 201 and STT 441 and STT 442)
          </p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <title>Textbook and course materials</title>

          <p>
            <pubtitle>An Introduction to Statistical Learning: With Applications in Python</pubtitle>
            by James, Witten, Hastie, Tibshirani, and Taylor. Available as a FREE download at <url href="https://statlearning.com/">https://statlearning.com/</url>
          </p>
          <p>
            Some additional reading for those interested, although we will not have any assignments from this book: <pubtitle>The Elements of Statistical Learning}. Hastie, Tibshirani, and Friedman</pubtitle>. Available as a FREE download <url href="http://www-stat.stanford.edu/ElemStatLearn">here</url>.
          </p>
        </li>
      </dl>
    </p>

    <!-- Use paragraphs to break apart subsections -->
    <paragraphs>
      <title>Websites</title>

      <p>
        <ul>
          <li> 
            <p>Content for the class will be posted on the course webpage:   <url href="https://msu-cmse-courses.github.io/CMSE381-F26/">msu-cmse-courses.github.io/CMSE381-S26/</url>  
              which can also be accessed from <url href="http://cmse.msu.edu/CMSE381/">cmse.msu.edu/CMSE381</url>. 
              Nearly every class will have a skeleton of slides, as well as a jupyter notebook for coding portions.  
           </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              The D2L website has your grades kept as up to date as possible. Note that any running class GPAs are approximate as long as some assignments' grades are still pending and they are meant to give the students an idea of their class performance as opposed to what their final GPA in the course is. Any accidental deviations in the distribution/calculation of the approximate running course GPAs on D2L will be corrected using the grades' distribution posted in the syllabus. When all the semester grades are in, the instructors will post the final calculated grades for the students to check. It is the students' responsibility to check that their grades were entered correctly and that their final grades are consistent with the distribution posted in the syllabus. 
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              We use Crowdmark (\url{https://crowdmark.com/}) for grading. You will have access to graded quizzes and tests from this website. Once we have the first quiz, you will get an invitation from the website to be able to upload your stuff.                
            </p>
          </li>
